<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $412.8 mln June 3.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $412.8 mln June 3.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $412.8 million deficit on June 3 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 3</p>
<p>Exports: $200.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $611.8 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $265 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $266.8 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $412.8 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $512.5 million</p>
<p>Imports: $918.2 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $589.3 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $543.1 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $359.5 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
